{"nodes": [{"id": "forge_manifest_manifest", "label": "Forge app manifest", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Modules, resources, remote, scopes and runtime for the Forge app. The app id is committed deliberately absent; tests/test_service.py checks HEAD."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_jira_projectpage", "label": "jira:projectPage delivery-value-dashboard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The product panel: resource main, resolver function, title Delivery & Value."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_connection_check_adminpage", "label": "jira:adminPage connection-check", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The probe, not the product. An adminPage because Forge permits one projectPage and because a page that dumps board contents belongs behind the admin gate."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_llm_brief_writer", "label": "llm module brief-writer (claude)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The brief is written by an Atlassian-hosted model with no egress, which is why item 3 does not send issue titles to a third party. Declaring it was a major version, landed while there were no external installs. ADR 0013."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_business_value_field", "label": "jira:customField Business Value (number)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Declared, not created: a customField module makes Jira create a locked field on install, needing no Administer Jira. Not readOnly and the app never writes it, so no write scope. An admin must add it to a screen; which levels count is orgConfig.valueFromHierarchy applied by the tools. ADR 0025."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_value_basis_field", "label": "jira:customField Value Basis (string)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Free text by design: nothing sizes, ranks or scores on it; intake.sequence carries it through and prints it beside the ordering's cost. An enumeration would be one join from a weight. In NEVER_SEND and FREE_TEXT_FIELDS so it never leaves the tenant. ADR 0027."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_candidate_field", "label": "jira:customField Candidate (string)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Candidacy is a state, not a type; every epic would sequence decisions already taken. Text because Forge cannot declare a checkbox and creating one needs Administer Jira; orgconfig.candidate_answer reads Yes/Y/True and reports anything else as unrecognised. orgConfig.askField lets a site point elsewhere. ADR 0028."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_tshirt_size_field", "label": "jira:customField T-Shirt Size (string)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A band is a selector, not a number: tshirt_scale builds S/M/L/XL from quartiles of the board's completed epics. Optional; needs eight completed epics rather than five. orgConfig.sizeField points at an existing field. ADR 0029."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_resolver_function", "label": "function resolver (index.handler, 1,024 MB)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loads the Python runtime from a memory snapshot to validate a sequencing request and answers facts, forecast, history and burndown route by route. 1,024 MB because measured RSS after load is 347 MB and an out-of-memory in a tenant would say nothing. ADR 0031."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_simulation_fn", "label": "function simulation-fn (900 s, 1,024 MB)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The consumer that computes sequencing (cubic, twelve asks 209 s) and the forecast under the platform ceiling rather than the resolver's 25 s. 900 is the ceiling not the need because Forge bills measured time; the ask cap guards against a run that cannot finish. Adding a function and consumer is minor, settled by the second probe."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_weekly_brief_fn", "label": "function weekly-brief-fn (120 s, 1,024 MB)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Must be its own function: the scheduled trigger once pointed at the resolver dispatcher, fired twice on 2026-08-24 and threw TypeError with nothing surfacing it. Confirmed working 2026-08-26 via a temporary fiveMinute interval. Runs the Python in-function since the facts route moved."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_scheduled_trigger_weekly_brief", "label": "scheduledTrigger weekly-brief", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Roadmap item 3; declared before it did anything because the permission is easier to argue for at listing time. Checks board, recipients and transport before any Jira call."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_simulation_consumer", "label": "consumer simulation-consumer (queue: simulations)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The queue the sequence and forecast resolvers push to. The queue name is QUEUE_KEY in forge/src/jobs.js and tests/test_service.py holds the strings together, because a misspelt queue is an event accepted by the platform and run by nothing."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_main_resource", "label": "resource main (static/dashboard/build)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Produced by make forge-static, git-ignored; build.py --split because the iframe CSP blocks inline style and script, seeded from forge/seed.json, bridge.js linked ahead of app.js."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_probe_resource", "label": "resource probe (static/probe)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bundled because @forge/bridge is CommonJS, so a Custom UI resource that calls invoke() has to be built rather than copied."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_calculator_remote", "label": "remote calculator (region-pinned baseUrl)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "baseUrl object of US/EU/GB Cloud Run URLs resolved per installation from the customer's residency setting so the app never picks a region; operations: [compute] both enables invokeRemote and declares no storage, protecting PINNED status. invokeRemote in index.js, not this declaration, attaches the invocation token. Changing the hostnames later is a major version. ADR 0012, ADR 0030."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_read_only_scopes", "label": "Read-only Jira scopes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "read:board-scope, read:epic (epics are not on a scrum board, ADR 0026), read:issue-details, read:jira-work, read:jira-user, read:project (the context picker's price, ADR 0009), read:sprint and read:jql (both demanded by forge lint for the sprint-issue endpoint; the app issues no JQL of its own). Union of granular and classic vocabularies, an OPEN item."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_send_notification_scope", "label": "scope send:notification:jira", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only way to send mail; keeps the brief inside Atlassian; grants no read or write of issue data and cannot address anyone outside the site. Non-read scopes live in an allow-list test with a justification. ADR 0014."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_storage_app_scope", "label": "scope storage:app", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The app's own key-value store for a board's recipient list; grants no Jira data access. The alternative, a project property, would have meant write access into the customer's project."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_runtime_nodejs24", "label": "app.runtime nodejs24.x, memoryMB 1024", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ran nodejs22.x until 2026-09-03, when an in-function forecast took twelve seconds against the probe's three; the Node version was the one variable left. Memory declared app-wide as well as per function so the log can say which held."}, {"id": "forge_manifest_egress_costs_badge", "label": "Egress costs the Runs on Atlassian badge", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The price of reaching one implementation of the forecast over a remote; since 2026-09-01 the tools also run unchanged under WebAssembly in a Forge function, so the calculator stands until that trade is taken and the badge is forfeit as a decision, not a discovery at listing time."}, {"id": "agent_tools_orgconfig_value_of", "label": "orgconfig.value_of()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_tools_orgconfig_candidate_answer", "label": "orgconfig.candidate_answer()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_tools_intake_tshirt_scale", "label": "intake.tshirt_scale()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "service_app_free_text_fields", "label": "app.FREE_TEXT_FIELDS", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "forge_src_index_handler", "label": "index.handler", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "forge_src_index_simulationconsumer", "label": "index.simulationConsumer", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "forge_src_index_weeklybrief", "label": "index.weeklyBrief", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "forge_src_index_invokeremote", "label": "invokeRemote in forge/src/index.js", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "forge_src_index_never_send", "label": "NEVER_SEND in forge/src/index.js", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "forge_src_jobs_queue_key", "label": "QUEUE_KEY in forge/src/jobs.js", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_test_service", "label": "tests/test_service.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "forge_manifest_manifest", "target": "forge_manifest_jira_projectpage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "forge_manifest_manifest", "target": "forge_manifest_connection_check_adminpage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "forge_manifest_connection_check_adminpage", "target": "forge_manifest_probe_resource", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "forge/manifest.yml", "source